# Godot Web Export Shared Runtime (Generic Setup)

Use a shared runtime for all web exports to avoid duplicating large binaries and
to standardize hosting. This rule applies to any game in this environment.

Authoritative version: `C:\Users\bruno\dev\Godot\.cursor\rules\godot-web-export-shared-runtime.mdc`

## Shared Runtime Contract

All games assume a central `_GODOT` folder exists **one level above** each game
export folder, containing:
- `godot.wasm`
- `godot.audio.worklet.js`
- `godot.audio.position.worklet.js`

No game-specific folder should contain its own `*.wasm` or audio worklet files.

## Folder Layout (Expected)

Example layout:

```
exports/
  _GODOT/
    godot.wasm
    godot.audio.worklet.js
    godot.audio.position.worklet.js
  game-a/
    game-a.html
    game-a.js
    game-a.pck
    icons/ or *.png
  game-b/
    game-b.html
    game-b.js
    game-b.pck
```

## HTML Shell Requirements (Custom Shell)

Use a custom HTML shell so exported files always point to the shared runtime.
The shell must:
- Include `$GODOT_URL` and `$GODOT_CONFIG` placeholders.
- Include splash UI markup (so the boot splash shows).
- Override `GODOT_CONFIG.executable` to `../_GODOT/godot`.
- Ensure `mainPack` is set (usually `<game>.pck`).
- Rewrite `fileSizes` so it includes `../_GODOT/godot.wasm` and **does not**
  reference `<game>.wasm` in the game folder.
- Initialize the engine with the shared wasm and preload the `.pck`.

### Working initialization pattern (shared runtime)

```
const GODOT_CONFIG = $GODOT_CONFIG;
const GODOT_SCRIPT = "$GODOT_URL";
const baseName = GODOT_SCRIPT.replace(/\.js$/, "");
const mainPack = GODOT_CONFIG.mainPack || (baseName + ".pck");
const sharedWasm = "../_GODOT/godot.wasm";

GODOT_CONFIG.mainPack = mainPack;
GODOT_CONFIG.executable = "../_GODOT/godot";

if (!GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes) {
  GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes = {};
}
const localWasm = baseName + ".wasm";
if (GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[localWasm]) {
  GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[sharedWasm] = GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[localWasm];
  delete GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[localWasm];
} else if (!GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[sharedWasm]) {
  GODOT_CONFIG.fileSizes[sharedWasm] = 0;
}

const engine = new Engine(GODOT_CONFIG);
Promise.all([
  engine.init(sharedWasm),
  engine.preloadFile(mainPack),
]).then(() => {
  return engine.start({
    args: ["--main-pack", mainPack],
    canvas: document.getElementById("canvas"),
  });
});
```

## Export Preset Requirements (Godot 4.x)

For each game:
- Set **Html / Custom Html Shell** to the shared custom shell file.
- Keep **Export Path** under a game-specific folder (e.g. `export/my_game/my_game.html`).
- Leave threads disabled unless your host supports COOP/COEP.
- Preset name does not matter; only the Web platform and the shell path do.

### Recommended preset export path

Use a nested folder so “Export All” produces the correct layout:

```
export/<game>/<game>.html
```

## Automated Cleanup (Export Plugin)

Add an `EditorExportPlugin` that runs on web exports and removes per-game runtime
artifacts from the export directory:
- `*.wasm`
- `*.wasm.debug`
- `*.audio.worklet.js`
- `*.audio.position.worklet.js`

This ensures “Export All” always yields only the allowed files per game.

Minimal plugin outline:

```
@tool
extends EditorExportPlugin

func _export_begin(features: PackedStringArray, _is_debug: bool, path: String, _flags: int) -> void:
	# Store export dir only for web exports
	pass

func _export_end() -> void:
	# Delete *.wasm and audio worklets from export dir
	pass
```

Enable the plugin in **Project Settings → Plugins** (or add it under
`[editor_plugins]` in `project.godot`).

## Files to Keep Per Game

Inside each game export folder, keep only:
- `*.html`
- `*.js`
- `*.pck`
- images (`*.png`, icons)

Everything else is centralized in `_GODOT`.

## Git Ignore Guidance

Do not ignore the entire export folder. Only ignore runtime artifacts:
- `**/*.wasm`
- `**/*.wasm.debug`

This keeps HTML/JS/PCK and images tracked while preventing per-game runtime files.

## Step-by-Step Setup for New Games

1) **Add a custom HTML shell** (e.g. `res://web_export_shell.html`) that:
   - Includes splash markup and uses the shared-runtime init pattern above.
2) **Add the export cleanup plugin** under `res://addons/<plugin>/` and enable it.
3) **Configure the Web preset**:
   - `Html / Custom Html Shell` → your shell file.
   - `Export Path` → `export/<game>/<game>.html`.
4) **Ensure shared runtime exists** at `export/_GODOT/` with the three runtime files.
5) **Export** using the Web preset (Export Project or Export All).

## When Runtime Changes

If Godot version or web export settings change:
- Regenerate the runtime once.
- Replace the shared files in `_GODOT`.
- Update any HTML shells if `fileSizes` or config structure changes.
